---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ModelInfo from '../../components/ModelInfo.astro';
import ToolMeta from '../../components/ToolMeta.astro';
---

<Layout title="RCWA — 1D Grating" description="Rigorous Coupled Wave Analysis for 1D periodic gratings. Compute reflection and transmission spectra via Fourier modal method.">
  <section class="widget-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/lab/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Lab</a>
      <h1>1D Grating <span class="gradient-text">RCWA</span></h1>
      <p class="widget-hero__subtitle">
        Rigorous Coupled Wave Analysis (Fourier modal method) for 1D binary
        gratings. Compute reflection R(λ) and transmission T(λ). Runs in-browser
        via Pyodide + <a href="https://github.com/alexysong/inkstone" target="_blank" rel="noopener">inkstone</a>.
        <br/><strong>First load downloads ~35 MB (Pyodide + numpy + scipy + inkstone) — cached after.</strong>
      </p>
      <ToolMeta slug="rcwa" name="RCWA — 1D Grating" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <ModelInfo status="Experimental">
    <dl>
      <dt>Model</dt>
      <dd>Rigorous Coupled Wave Analysis (Fourier modal method). Fields are expanded in plane-wave harmonics of the grating period; an eigenvalue problem is solved in each layer. Powered by <a href="https://github.com/alexysong/inkstone" target="_blank" rel="noopener">inkstone</a> via Pyodide.</dd>
      <dt>Assumptions</dt>
      <dd>1D periodicity, infinite lateral extent, plane-wave illumination, isotropic materials in each layer.</dd>
      <dt>Validity</dt>
      <dd>Exact in the limit of sufficient Fourier orders. Convergence should be checked by increasing the truncation order — especially for metallic gratings where convergence can be slow.</dd>
      <dt>Limitations</dt>
      <dd>1D gratings only (no 2D periodicity). Browser memory limits the practical number of Fourier orders. First load downloads ~35 MB (Pyodide + numpy + scipy + inkstone).</dd>
      <dt>References</dt>
      <dd>M. G. Moharam &amp; T. K. Gaylord, J. Opt. Soc. Am. <strong>71</strong>, 811 (1981); L. Li, J. Opt. Soc. Am. A <strong>14</strong>, 2758 (1997).</dd>
    </dl>
  </ModelInfo>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="module-bar card" role="radiogroup" aria-label="RCWA module">
        <span class="module-bar__label">Module</span>
        <div class="module-bar__grid">
          <button type="button" class="module-card active" id="module-rcwa-1d" role="radio" aria-checked="true">
            <span class="module-card__name">1D-RCWA</span>
            <span class="module-card__desc">Binary 1D gratings &middot; R/T spectra</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="module-card" id="module-blazed" role="radio" aria-checked="false">
            <span class="module-card__name">Blazed gratings</span>
            <span class="module-card__desc">Echelette geometry &middot; grating equation &amp; Littrow blaze</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="widget-layout" id="module-panel-rcwa-1d">
        <!-- ===== Controls ===== -->
        <div class="controls card">
          <h3 class="controls-title">Parameters</h3>
          <h3>Grating</h3>
          <div class="param-group">
            <div class="fields">
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-period">&Lambda; period [nm]</label>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-period" inputmode="decimal" value="700">
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-thickness">d thickness [nm]</label>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-thickness" inputmode="decimal" value="300">
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-width">Ridge width [nm]</label>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-width" inputmode="decimal" value="350">
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <div class="field-label-with-info">
                  <label for="p-numg">Harmonics</label>
                  <button class="field-info" type="button" aria-label="Harmonics info" aria-describedby="harmonics-tooltip">i</button>
                  <span class="field-tooltip" id="harmonics-tooltip" role="tooltip">Number of Fourier orders used in the RCWA expansion. Higher values improve convergence for sharp or high-contrast gratings, but make the calculation slower.</span>
                </div>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-numg" inputmode="numeric" value="25">
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3>Materials &epsilon; = n&sup2;</h3>
          <div class="param-group">
            <div class="eps-fields">
              <div class="eps-field">
                <span class="eps-label">Top</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-top-re" inputmode="decimal" value="1.0" title="Re(ε)">
                <span class="plus">+ i</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-top-im" inputmode="decimal" value="0.0" title="Im(ε)">
              </div>
              <div class="eps-field">
                <span class="eps-label">Ridge</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-ridge-re" inputmode="decimal" value="5.76">
                <span class="plus">+ i</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-ridge-im" inputmode="decimal" value="0.0">
              </div>
              <div class="eps-field">
                <span class="eps-label">Groove</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-groove-re" inputmode="decimal" value="1.0">
                <span class="plus">+ i</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-groove-im" inputmode="decimal" value="0.0">
              </div>
              <div class="eps-field">
                <span class="eps-label">Substrate</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-sub-re" inputmode="decimal" value="2.25">
                <span class="plus">+ i</span>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-eps-sub-im" inputmode="decimal" value="0.0">
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="preset-row">
              <button class="preset-btn" data-preset="dielectric">Si grating</button>
              <button class="preset-btn" data-preset="metal">Au grating</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3>Incidence</h3>
          <div class="param-group">
            <div class="fields">
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-theta">&theta; [deg]</label>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-theta" inputmode="decimal" value="0">
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-pol">Polarization</label>
                <select class="field-input" id="p-pol">
                  <option value="s" selected>s (TE)</option>
                  <option value="p">p (TM)</option>
                </select>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3>Wavelength sweep</h3>
          <div class="param-group">
            <div class="fields">
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-lmin">&lambda;<sub>min</sub> [nm]</label>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-lmin" inputmode="decimal" value="400">
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-lmax">&lambda;<sub>max</sub> [nm]</label>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-lmax" inputmode="decimal" value="1200">
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="p-npts">Points</label>
                <input type="text" class="field-input" id="p-npts" inputmode="numeric" value="60">
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <button class="run-btn" id="run-btn" disabled data-umami-event="rcwa-run">Loading solver…</button>

          <p class="theory-note">
            <strong>RCWA (Fourier modal method).</strong>
            Expands fields in plane-wave harmonics of the grating period and
            solves the eigenvalue problem in each layer. Diffraction orders
            couple through the Fourier decomposition of &epsilon;(x).
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- ===== Chart ===== -->
        <div class="chart-panel card">
          <div class="chart-header">
            <span class="chart-title">Reflection / Transmission spectrum</span>
            <span class="chart-header__right">
              <button id="dl-png" class="share-btn" title="Download chart as PNG" data-umami-event="rcwa-export" data-umami-event-format="png">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/><path d="m21 15-5-5L5 21"/></svg>
                PNG
              </button>
              <button id="dl-csv" class="share-btn" title="Download R,T data as CSV" data-umami-event="rcwa-export" data-umami-event-format="csv">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                CSV
              </button>
              <button id="share-btn" class="share-btn" title="Copy shareable link" data-umami-event="share" data-umami-event-page="rcwa">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg>
                Share
              </button>
              <span class="chart-status" id="status">Initializing…</span>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="chart-wrap">
            <canvas id="rt-canvas" aria-label="Reflection and transmission spectrum"></canvas>
          </div>
          <div class="progress-bar"><div class="progress-fill" id="progress-fill"></div></div>
          <section class="rcwa-conventions" aria-labelledby="rcwa-schematic-title">
            <div class="rcwa-conventions__header">
              <span class="rcwa-conventions__title" id="rcwa-schematic-title">Geometry and solver conventions</span>
              <span class="rcwa-conventions__tag">1D periodic, &phi; = 0</span>
            </div>
            <div class="rcwa-conventions__body">
              <svg class="rcwa-schematic" viewBox="0 0 820 350" role="img" aria-labelledby="rcwa-svg-title rcwa-svg-desc">
                <title id="rcwa-svg-title">RCWA 1D grating geometry convention</title>
                <desc id="rcwa-svg-desc">A 1D grating with x-period Lambda, invariant y direction, z layer stacking, top superstrate, finite patterned grating, substrate, incident wave vector, incidence angle theta, and TE/TM polarization definitions.</desc>
                <defs>
                  <marker id="rcwa-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto-start-reverse" markerUnits="strokeWidth">
                    <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></path>
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="rcwa-arrow-filled" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto" markerUnits="strokeWidth">
                    <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z" fill="currentColor"></path>
                  </marker>
                  <linearGradient id="rcwa-top-fill" x1="0" x2="0" y1="0" y2="1">
                    <stop offset="0" stop-color="#DBEAFE" stop-opacity="0.55"></stop>
                    <stop offset="1" stop-color="#DBEAFE" stop-opacity="0.16"></stop>
                  </linearGradient>
                  <linearGradient id="rcwa-sub-fill" x1="0" x2="0" y1="0" y2="1">
                    <stop offset="0" stop-color="#D1FAE5" stop-opacity="0.32"></stop>
                    <stop offset="1" stop-color="#D1FAE5" stop-opacity="0.72"></stop>
                  </linearGradient>
                  <pattern id="rcwa-sub-hatch" width="8" height="8" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(45)">
                    <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.08" stroke-width="2"></line>
                  </pattern>
                </defs>

                <rect class="rcwa-svg-bg" x="0" y="0" width="820" height="350" rx="10"></rect>
                <rect class="rcwa-superstrate" x="150" y="38" width="570" height="90" rx="4"></rect>
                <rect class="rcwa-groove" x="150" y="128" width="570" height="88"></rect>
                <rect class="rcwa-substrate" x="150" y="216" width="570" height="76" rx="4"></rect>
                <rect class="rcwa-hatch" x="150" y="216" width="570" height="76"></rect>

                <line class="rcwa-interface" x1="150" y1="128" x2="720" y2="128"></line>
                <line class="rcwa-interface" x1="150" y1="216" x2="720" y2="216"></line>
                <line class="rcwa-boundary" x1="150" y1="64" x2="150" y2="292"></line>
                <line class="rcwa-boundary" x1="340" y1="64" x2="340" y2="306"></line>
                <line class="rcwa-boundary" x1="530" y1="64" x2="530" y2="306"></line>
                <line class="rcwa-boundary" x1="720" y1="64" x2="720" y2="292"></line>

                <g class="rcwa-ridges">
                  <rect x="150" y="128" width="88" height="88" rx="3"></rect>
                  <rect x="340" y="128" width="88" height="88" rx="3"></rect>
                  <rect x="530" y="128" width="88" height="88" rx="3"></rect>
                </g>
                <g class="rcwa-material-labels">
                  <text x="384" y="177" text-anchor="middle">Ridge</text>
                  <text x="479" y="177" text-anchor="middle">Groove</text>
                </g>

                <text class="rcwa-label rcwa-label-strong" x="132" y="70" text-anchor="end">Superstrate / top</text>
                <text class="rcwa-label" x="132" y="91" text-anchor="end">semi-infinite input</text>
                <text class="rcwa-label rcwa-label-strong" x="132" y="165" text-anchor="end">Patterned layer</text>
                <text class="rcwa-label" x="132" y="186" text-anchor="end">ridge + groove</text>
                <text class="rcwa-label rcwa-label-strong" x="132" y="252" text-anchor="end">Substrate</text>
                <text class="rcwa-label" x="132" y="273" text-anchor="end">semi-infinite output</text>

                <g class="rcwa-dimension">
                  <line x1="340" y1="308" x2="530" y2="308" marker-start="url(#rcwa-arrow)" marker-end="url(#rcwa-arrow)"></line>
                  <text x="435" y="327" text-anchor="middle">&Lambda; period along x</text>
                  <line x1="340" y1="204" x2="428" y2="204" marker-start="url(#rcwa-arrow)" marker-end="url(#rcwa-arrow)"></line>
                  <text x="384" y="196" text-anchor="middle">ridge width</text>
                  <line x1="754" y1="128" x2="754" y2="216" marker-start="url(#rcwa-arrow)" marker-end="url(#rcwa-arrow)"></line>
                  <text x="771" y="172" transform="rotate(90 771 172)" text-anchor="middle">thickness d</text>
                </g>

                <g class="rcwa-incidence">
                  <line class="rcwa-wave" x1="276" y1="50" x2="335" y2="122" marker-end="url(#rcwa-arrow-filled)"></line>
                  <path d="M340 96 A32 32 0 0 0 319 104"></path>
                  <text x="258" y="86">k<tspan baseline-shift="sub" font-size="10">inc</tspan></text>
                  <text x="323" y="92">&theta;</text>
                  <text x="352" y="76">surface normal</text>
                </g>
              </svg>

              <ul class="rcwa-convention-list">
                <li><strong>x</strong> is periodic with period &Lambda;; <strong>y</strong> is invariant along the ridge direction.</li>
                <li><strong>z</strong> follows the layer stack from top/superstrate to substrate.</li>
                <li>The incident plane wave enters from the top region; &theta; is measured from the surface normal in the x-z plane.</li>
                <li><strong>s/TE</strong> means E along y; <strong>p/TM</strong> means E lies in the x-z incidence plane.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== Blazed gratings module ===== -->
      <div id="module-panel-blazed" hidden>
        <div class="widget-layout">
          <!-- Controls -->
          <div class="controls card">
            <h3 class="controls-title">Parameters</h3>
            <h3>Grating</h3>
            <div class="param-group">
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="bz-density">Groove density [/mm]</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="bz-density" inputmode="decimal" value="600">
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="bz-blaze">Blaze &gamma; [deg]</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="bz-blaze" inputmode="decimal" value="10">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Illumination</h3>
            <div class="param-group">
              <div class="fields">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="bz-lambda">&lambda; [nm]</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="bz-lambda" inputmode="decimal" value="550">
                </div>
                <input type="range" class="bz-range" id="bz-lambda-slider" min="300" max="900" step="1" value="550" aria-label="Wavelength slider">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="bz-theta">Incidence &theta;<sub>i</sub> [deg]</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="bz-theta" inputmode="decimal" value="0">
                </div>
                <input type="range" class="bz-range" id="bz-theta-slider" min="-80" max="80" step="0.5" value="0" aria-label="Incidence angle slider">
                <div class="field">
                  <label for="bz-ngrooves">Grooves N</label>
                  <input type="text" class="field-input" id="bz-ngrooves" inputmode="numeric" value="1200">
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="theory-note">
              <strong>Blazed (echelette) grating.</strong>
              Analytic grating equation d(sin&thinsp;&theta;<sub>i</sub> + sin&thinsp;&theta;<sub>m</sub>) = m&lambda;,
              Littrow blaze, and derived dispersion. Facets tilted by &gamma; steer
              power into the order whose angle matches the facet reflection.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Interactive result box -->
          <div class="bz-results">
            <div class="chart-panel card">
              <div class="chart-header">
                <span class="chart-title">Diffraction orders &amp; blaze</span>
                <span class="chart-header__right">
                  <span class="bz-legend">
                    <span class="bz-legend-item"><span class="bz-legend-swatch bz-legend-swatch--incident"></span>Incident</span>
                    <span class="bz-legend-item"><span class="bz-legend-swatch bz-legend-swatch--blaze"></span>Blaze direction</span>
                    <span class="bz-legend-item bz-legend-warning" id="bz-legend-warning" hidden></span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="chart-status" id="bz-status"></span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <div class="chart-wrap">
                <canvas id="bz-canvas" aria-label="Blazed grating diffraction orders diagram"></canvas>
              </div>
              <div class="bz-export-bar">
                <span class="bz-export-label">Export</span>
                <button id="bz-dl-png" class="share-btn" title="Download diagram as PNG">
                  <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/><path d="m21 15-5-5L5 21"/></svg>
                  PNG
                </button>
                <button id="bz-dl-csv" class="share-btn" title="Download all diffraction orders as CSV">
                  <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                  CSV
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>

            <section class="output-card card">
              <div class="bz-order-select stat--wide">
                <span class="bz-order-select__label">Order m</span>
                <div class="bz-order-btns" id="bz-order-btns" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Diffraction order"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Line spacing info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Groove period d = 1/(groove density). Sets the grating equation scale.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Line spacing d</span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-d">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit">nm</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Diffraction angle info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Diffraction angle of the selected order m from the grating equation d(sin θ_i + sin θ_m) = mλ. Shows "evanescent" if the order does not propagate.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Diffraction angle &theta;<sub>m</sub></span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-thetam">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit" id="bz-u-thetam">order m</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Littrow info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Littrow blaze angle θ_B = arcsin(mλ/2d): the configuration where incidence and diffraction coincide.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Littrow blaze &theta;<sub>B</sub></span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-littrow">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit" id="bz-u-littrow">order m</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Blaze wavelength info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Blaze wavelength λ_b = 2d·sin γ / m at which the grating set at blaze angle γ is most efficient in order m (Littrow).</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Blaze &lambda; at &gamma;</span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-blaze">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit">nm</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Angular dispersion info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Angular dispersion dθ_m/dλ = m/(d·cos θ_m) for the selected order.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Angular dispersion</span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-disp">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit">mrad/nm</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Free spectral range info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Free spectral range FSR = λ/m: the wavelength interval before the next order overlaps.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Free spectral range</span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-fsr">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit">nm</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Resolving power info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Theoretical resolving power R = λ/Δλ = m·N, with N the number of illuminated grooves.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Resolving power R</span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-r">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit">m &middot; N</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Echelle info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">An echelle grating is a blazed grating with a large blaze angle (γ &gt; 45°) used in high diffraction orders.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Echelle (&gamma; &gt; 45&deg;)</span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-echelle">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit">regime</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat">
                <button class="stat-info" type="button" aria-label="Propagating orders info">i<span class="stat-tooltip" role="tooltip">Number of diffraction orders that propagate (|sin θ_m| ≤ 1) for the current geometry. Select one with the Order m buttons.</span></button>
                <span class="stat-label">Propagating orders</span>
                <span class="stat-value" id="bz-v-norders">&mdash;</span>
                <span class="stat-unit">total</span>
              </div>
            </section>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="references card">
          <h4>Reference</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><em>Blazed grating</em>, Wikipedia &mdash; grating equation, Littrow configuration, blaze condition and echelle gratings. <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blazed_grating" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blazed_grating</a></li>
